  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Item 1b: delete the three handler files, their DI lines, their tests, and their ArchTests DEF-JOBS rows; update the handler table in jobs-architecture.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Item 2: make StartupDiagnostics' expected list equal the registered handlers' JobTypes (drop ProcessEmailToDocument, BatchProcessEmails and the deleted three); prefer deriving it from the registered `IJobHandler`s if that removes the duplicated list with no new surface.</step>
    <step order="3">Item 4: rewrite the listed lines of DOCUMENT-PROFILE-AND-AI-EXECUTION-MODELS.md to describe the direct-Action spine (`ProfileViaLinearActionAsync`, #919), with the node path as the null-seam fallback.</step>
    <step order="4">Item 5a: change both enqueue sites; write DocumentProfileIdempotencyKeyTests proving the email path and the upload path produce the same key and the handler processes one profile for the pair.</step>
    <step order="5">Item 6: add the ConsumerTypes constants + `All` entries; run RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheckTests.</step>
    <step order="6">`dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, `dotnet test` (unit + ArchTests incl. WorkloadPlacementDocDriftTests); start the API locally and confirm no StartupDiagnostics warning names a missing handler.</step>
