  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">DocumentProcessingJobHandler, ProfileSummaryJobHandler and EmailAnalysisJobHandler no longer exist in src or tests, and no DI line, diagnostics entry or ArchTests row names them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On startup, StartupDiagnostics logs no warning naming a missing handler (FR-03a).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same document enqueued by the email path and by the upload path, then both JobContracts carry the identical `ProfileIdempotencyKey(documentId)` key with MaxAttempts 3 and the handler produces one profile (FR-03b regression test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a different document id yields a different key (no false dedup).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ConsumerTypes.All contains `agreement-classify` and `nda-review` (and `nda-standard-summary` if its row exists); RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheckTests pass with no drift for them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The profile doc no longer describes the node playbook as the primary path at the listed lines.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build passes; all unit tests and ArchTests (incl. WorkloadPlacementDocDriftTests) pass (FR-03a, FR-03f).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

